Answer: An int to char conversion requires explicit casting. Example:

```java
int value = 65;
char ch = (char) value;
```

The resulting character corresponds to the character represented by that numeric code.

Answer: ```java
public class Main {
public static void main(String[] args) {
int value = 65;
char ch = (char) value;
System.out.println(ch);
}
}
```

Sample Input: No input Output: A The numeric value 65 is converted into its corresponding character.

