Answer: Widening: Smaller/compatible type → larger type Usually automatic Also called implicit type casting Example:

```java
byte a = 10;
int b = a;
```

Narrowing: Larger type → smaller type Requires explicit casting May cause data loss Also called explicit type casting Example:

```java
int a = 100;
byte b = (byte) a;
```

So, widening is generally performed automatically, while narrowing requires the programmer to explicitly specify the conversion.
